From 48e4fbe65c40296fa03f2354b739b27d60df4287 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:58:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 183/193] urltest: one tester for all groups, several URLs,
 median of a cycle

- urls: the URLs of the tests, one a round in turn, numbered by the clock so that
  every group of the process tests with the same URL in the same round. A member
  that does not answer the URL of the round is tested once with the next one: it is
  unavailable when two URLs do not answer, not one.
- The delay of a member is the median of the last rounds, as many as there are URLs
  (one per operator), kept in the history storage of the process: a URL that did not
  answer leaves no sample, one stray test does not move the choice. A failure drops
  the samples. A delay test the Clash API asks for, with its own URL, answers its
  client and leaves such a median alone.
- One URL tester for the process: a test of an outbound with a URL another group
  asked for is waited for, not run again; tests whose connections begin at the same
  first server (the outbound itself, or the end of its chain of detours) begin 2 s
  apart, so twenty members behind one detour do not send it a burst of TLS hellos;
  tests through different first servers run at once. The test of a member whose
  connections fail and the download test wait for its first server too.
